 "text": "Hi, how are you holding her? It depends on the thin film varnish you used, usually seven days. If it feels dry only on the clock tick it might be worth waiting longer. Lovely. Hang it where it can get air, but not in direct light. A hall or garage is good. You can use a very light room with the window closed and open a door. Keep the room on, just not all day. Rub it with your fingernail, not hard, and see how it feels. It should stop leaving a mark.",
